WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.182 --> 00:00:04.269
- Evolve.
- Evolve.

00:00:04.269 --> 00:00:05.277
- Evolve.
- Evolve.

00:00:05.277 --> 00:00:06.110
- Evolve.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.363
- Hello Believe Nation, today
we're going to talk about

00:00:08.363 --> 00:00:10.622
how you need to evolve.

00:00:10.622 --> 00:00:12.199
And as always guys, if you hear something

00:00:12.199 --> 00:00:13.582
that really resonates with you,

00:00:13.582 --> 00:00:15.264
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:15.264 --> 00:00:17.743
put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:17.743 --> 00:00:19.318
And when you write it down yourself,

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:23.485
it's much more likely to
stick with you as well, enjoy!

00:00:25.412 --> 00:00:28.329
(energizing music)

00:00:34.846 --> 00:00:36.813
- You can only hope that
as a writer you start

00:00:36.813 --> 00:00:38.666
trying different things and,

00:00:38.666 --> 00:00:41.620
you try different chords or
different structures of songs.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.329
Different beats that you've
never really explored

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:45.746
that path before.

00:00:46.839 --> 00:00:47.672
You know,

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.149
I think,

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:52.385
having always been a writer first,

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.903
I'm obsessed with the syncopation of

00:00:54.903 --> 00:00:58.022
the way that words sound when
they're said a certain way.

00:00:58.022 --> 00:01:01.713
And, once I've done something
once, I always want to go

00:01:01.713 --> 00:01:05.880
to a different direction and
never repeat myself so...

00:01:06.743 --> 00:01:08.926
As a writer I think that I've always hoped

00:01:08.926 --> 00:01:13.380
that my music would
constantly be changing because

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.440
you never want to make
the same album twice,

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.440
the same song twice and,

00:01:18.962 --> 00:01:22.798
my greatest hope has been that as I grow,

00:01:22.798 --> 00:01:25.859
my fans will grow up
with me, and as I change

00:01:25.859 --> 00:01:28.427
and my life changes, my
music will change as well.

00:01:28.427 --> 00:01:30.260
So wish me luck there.

00:01:31.099 --> 00:01:34.178
- When I was younger I didn't
really know that you could

00:01:34.178 --> 00:01:35.571
just get better at things.

00:01:35.571 --> 00:01:37.838
'Cause I think we're so
used to the idea that

00:01:37.838 --> 00:01:40.588
you're talented at something and,

00:01:42.199 --> 00:01:44.192
it's sort of fixed.

00:01:44.192 --> 00:01:48.433
The idea that, oh, he's just
a good singer, you know.

00:01:48.433 --> 00:01:52.885
And, even with singing, I've
gotten better at singing

00:01:52.885 --> 00:01:54.606
as I've gotten older.

00:01:54.606 --> 00:01:57.713
I wasn't singing in a way
that was sustainable and

00:01:57.713 --> 00:01:59.511
I wasn't breathing right, I wasn't doing

00:01:59.511 --> 00:02:00.832
a bunch of things correctly.

00:02:00.832 --> 00:02:03.368
I realized that there was a ceiling

00:02:03.368 --> 00:02:07.333
that I couldn't crack
through unless I actually

00:02:07.333 --> 00:02:10.863
studied and worked under
a coach to get better.

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:12.350
And,

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.346
this idea that things are just fixed

00:02:15.346 --> 00:02:17.301
is proven not to be the case.

00:02:17.301 --> 00:02:19.399
You can get better at
things, you can grow.

00:02:19.399 --> 00:02:22.106
And even people that are innately talented

00:02:22.106 --> 00:02:24.768
still need to go beyond

00:02:24.768 --> 00:02:27.555
that basic talent that
they have and cultivate it.

00:02:27.555 --> 00:02:30.500
- I've had to evolve so many times.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.180
I've had to change and grow so many times!

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:37.186
There's been times where
I've made such huge mistakes

00:02:37.186 --> 00:02:38.943
in my network marketing career.

00:02:38.943 --> 00:02:41.200
Damaged relationships, done things that

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.052
I wish I could go back and
change, but I couldn't.

00:02:44.052 --> 00:02:46.452
So I could either live there,

00:02:46.452 --> 00:02:50.768
or I could use that information
to grow and become better.

00:02:50.768 --> 00:02:53.886
See I've been involved for
25 years and I promise you,

00:02:53.886 --> 00:02:57.757
every year that we're engaged,
we're working together,

00:02:57.757 --> 00:03:00.669
every year you're going to see
me get a little bit better,

00:03:00.669 --> 00:03:01.868
and a little bit better.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:03.817
And most of the time I'm
not going to hit my goals,

00:03:03.817 --> 00:03:05.327
but then I'm going to
get a little bit better,

00:03:05.327 --> 00:03:08.563
and a little bit better
and compounded over time,

00:03:08.563 --> 00:03:09.998
you'll see noticeable results.

00:03:09.998 --> 00:03:11.786
Anybody that knows me knows
that I'm a different person

00:03:11.786 --> 00:03:15.054
than I was five years ago,
10 years ago, 15 years ago.

00:03:15.054 --> 00:03:16.872
Certainly 25 years ago.

00:03:16.872 --> 00:03:20.005
18 jobs, you know, barely surviving.

00:03:20.005 --> 00:03:22.031
So give yourself some grace.

00:03:22.031 --> 00:03:25.430
Understand that nothing is ever finished

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.355
while you're still alive.

00:03:27.355 --> 00:03:28.832
- So after you've been through the good,

00:03:28.832 --> 00:03:32.086
the bad, the ugly, what do
you know for sure about life?

00:03:32.086 --> 00:03:33.472
- That it moves on.

00:03:33.472 --> 00:03:35.135
- Everybody says that.
- The truth.

00:03:35.135 --> 00:03:36.424
- Just everybody's answer.
- It's the truth.

00:03:36.424 --> 00:03:39.293
That it moves on and it
keeps going, and guess what,

00:03:39.293 --> 00:03:42.206
it's going to move on and keep
going with or without you.

00:03:42.206 --> 00:03:44.617
So you know you better
adjust to the changes

00:03:44.617 --> 00:03:48.349
'cause if you don't adjust to
the changes, you stay stuck

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:50.876
in the way that you've been moving,

00:03:50.876 --> 00:03:52.415
you're going to keep
getting what you've been

00:03:52.415 --> 00:03:53.850
getting out of life,
and that's not the way

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.161
life is meant to be lived.

00:03:55.161 --> 00:03:57.494
Life is meant to be lived...

00:03:58.345 --> 00:03:59.727
You got to constantly evolve.

00:03:59.727 --> 00:04:01.598
You know change is the basis of growth.

00:04:01.598 --> 00:04:03.578
And growth is the basis of life.

00:04:03.578 --> 00:04:05.517
If you're not constantly
changing, you're not growing.

00:04:05.517 --> 00:04:07.048
If you're not growing
then what are you doing?

00:04:07.048 --> 00:04:09.336
You're dying, you're not doing nothing.

00:04:09.336 --> 00:04:11.145
So that's why when you
look at certain people man,

00:04:11.145 --> 00:04:13.665
and you see them, and they're
40-something years old,

00:04:13.665 --> 00:04:16.467
they washed up, 'cause
they still trying to live

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:18.112
the way they were when
they were in their 20s

00:04:18.112 --> 00:04:20.006
and their 30s, nothing
about them has grown.

00:04:20.006 --> 00:04:21.221
Nothing about them has evolved.

00:04:21.221 --> 00:04:23.885
Their mindset hasn't grown,
their mindset hasn't evolved.

00:04:23.885 --> 00:04:25.521
It's still hanging around the same people

00:04:25.521 --> 00:04:27.030
they was hanging around when they were

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.752
in their 20s doing nothing.

00:04:28.752 --> 00:04:30.531
So guess what, if you're
hanging around the same people

00:04:30.531 --> 00:04:32.403
that you were hanging around
in your 20s doing nothing,

00:04:32.403 --> 00:04:34.013
guess what you going to
be doing in your 30s?

00:04:34.013 --> 00:04:36.073
Nothing, so guess what you
going to be doing in your 40s?

00:04:36.073 --> 00:04:36.906
Nothing.

00:04:36.906 --> 00:04:38.403
So you got to understand, life moves on.

00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:40.288
Father time don't wait for nobody man,

00:04:40.288 --> 00:04:42.470
and when it's over, it's over.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:44.434
When you're 40-something
years old and you look back

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:48.751
and you're like damn, I wasted
all that time doing nothing.

00:04:48.751 --> 00:04:49.634
You know?

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:52.507
Life moved on and I didn't move with it.

00:04:52.507 --> 00:04:54.161
Now you just a washed individual.

00:04:54.161 --> 00:04:56.474
You don't got nobody to
blame for that but yourself.

00:04:56.474 --> 00:04:59.518
- But you came up with the
Waka Flocka record to this,

00:04:59.518 --> 00:05:01.151
there's like a big
difference in your style,

00:05:01.151 --> 00:05:03.156
in your approach, what's
the reason for that?

00:05:03.156 --> 00:05:05.936
- Probably because we grow
and evolution is beautiful

00:05:05.936 --> 00:05:08.585
and like, I want to be iconic
and great and I borderline

00:05:08.585 --> 00:05:11.133
am iconic, and I am great so it's like,

00:05:11.133 --> 00:05:13.172
the only thing left to do
- Tell me how you really feel.

00:05:13.172 --> 00:05:15.497
- Is to just evolve and continue to do so,

00:05:15.497 --> 00:05:17.414
and I'm responsible for

00:05:18.425 --> 00:05:21.744
possibly bringing rock and
roll in general into hip hop

00:05:21.744 --> 00:05:24.658
within our generation and
making that whole wave

00:05:24.658 --> 00:05:27.775
a cool thing, and
influencing all those artists

00:05:27.775 --> 00:05:29.511
when we were doing those
festivals back together

00:05:29.511 --> 00:05:33.548
in the 2012, and 2011, 2010
years when Wild Boy was

00:05:33.548 --> 00:05:35.639
a thing and when so
many other mixtape songs

00:05:35.639 --> 00:05:37.563
that I was doing were a thing so like yes,

00:05:37.563 --> 00:05:40.465
when I brought what I brought
in and everyone else took it,

00:05:40.465 --> 00:05:44.105
I do what all trendsetters
do and I just set a new trend

00:05:44.105 --> 00:05:48.962
and do on to the next thing
and let them keep doing that.

00:05:48.962 --> 00:05:51.267
- Dream Team Minaj says, "I
love you, but I'm curious

00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:53.566
"why did you change your rapping
style from the comeup days

00:05:53.566 --> 00:05:55.566
"to today, I love both."

00:05:56.965 --> 00:06:00.215
- I don't think I changed my rap style.

00:06:01.598 --> 00:06:03.990
I think you guys were
just starting to hear me,

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:07.150
and you didn't hear all
of me yet, that's it.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:10.509
I've always been into
being weird a little bit.

00:06:10.509 --> 00:06:12.131
But,

00:06:12.131 --> 00:06:14.419
I think what people really
mean is that they think

00:06:14.419 --> 00:06:16.510
that I've changed my persona.

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:17.343
And,

00:06:18.538 --> 00:06:21.512
life is about growth and change, and,

00:06:21.512 --> 00:06:24.962
I don't want to remain the
same for my whole life.

00:06:24.962 --> 00:06:27.762
I want to be able to change and

00:06:27.762 --> 00:06:30.512
you know I respect the people who

00:06:31.867 --> 00:06:32.991
loved

00:06:32.991 --> 00:06:35.559
'07 Nicki, and I'm definitely going to

00:06:35.559 --> 00:06:38.682
give you some stuff on Pink Friday.

00:06:38.682 --> 00:06:40.530
I'm not forgetting anybody.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:43.452
But I just also have to be true to me.

00:06:43.452 --> 00:06:47.509
And the truth is, I started
seeing different things,

00:06:47.509 --> 00:06:49.482
I started going different
places, I started

00:06:49.482 --> 00:06:52.810
eating different things, I can't...

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:55.919
It would be fraudulent to rap the same way

00:06:55.919 --> 00:06:58.106
and look the same way,
act the same way because

00:06:58.106 --> 00:07:00.485
I am not the same, period.

00:07:00.485 --> 00:07:01.318
I don't know to...

00:07:01.318 --> 00:07:03.368
- Well everyone has their
different belief systems.

00:07:03.368 --> 00:07:06.975
I think everyone has their
different opinions of

00:07:06.975 --> 00:07:08.899
those types of things
that you talked about.

00:07:08.899 --> 00:07:10.959
Certainly as an athlete, I care very much

00:07:10.959 --> 00:07:14.484
what I put into my body, I
think that, I'm 38 years old.

00:07:14.484 --> 00:07:16.627
I'm not 22 anymore.
- You look good.

00:07:16.627 --> 00:07:17.668
(chuckling)

00:07:17.668 --> 00:07:18.777
- You're very sweet, thank you.

00:07:18.777 --> 00:07:20.589
You know, all those things are important.

00:07:20.589 --> 00:07:23.077
And all the little things
add up to be big things so

00:07:23.077 --> 00:07:25.885
when I'm trying to accomplish
things professionally that,

00:07:25.885 --> 00:07:29.297
you know, in a lot of ways, I'm
in unchartered territory so,

00:07:29.297 --> 00:07:31.576
I've got to do things
differently, and I got to evolve

00:07:31.576 --> 00:07:34.350
over time, I've got to,
things that may have worked

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:35.902
in the past maybe don't
work as you move forward.

00:07:35.902 --> 00:07:38.059
So the lessons that I've
learned through my own

00:07:38.059 --> 00:07:39.843
trial and error, I think I'm at that point

00:07:39.843 --> 00:07:40.922
in my career where I'm very efficient

00:07:40.922 --> 00:07:42.974
with what I'm doing so,
I try to eat healthy,

00:07:42.974 --> 00:07:44.347
I try to get the right amount of rest.

00:07:44.347 --> 00:07:46.355
I try to do the right types of exercise

00:07:46.355 --> 00:07:48.280
so I can be on the field
and be available to my team.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:51.341
I try to be as productive
this time in my career

00:07:51.341 --> 00:07:52.746
as I was earlier.

00:07:52.746 --> 00:07:55.762
- Sure as we all have to
set goals for ourselves,

00:07:55.762 --> 00:07:59.095
I mean, our planned destination is to be

00:08:00.537 --> 00:08:01.640
busy.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:02.931
And,

00:08:02.931 --> 00:08:03.935
to,

00:08:03.935 --> 00:08:06.214
adjust to whatever you,

00:08:06.214 --> 00:08:08.243
whatever you're introduced to.

00:08:08.243 --> 00:08:10.491
And what I mean by that
is OK, as an entertainer,

00:08:10.491 --> 00:08:13.465
I started off as a singer.

00:08:13.465 --> 00:08:15.919
You know I grew to become
a dancer and a performer.

00:08:15.919 --> 00:08:18.157
After becoming a performer
then I became an actor.

00:08:18.157 --> 00:08:20.339
After becoming an actor
I became an entrepreneur.

00:08:20.339 --> 00:08:23.156
After becoming an entrepreneur
I became an entertainer

00:08:23.156 --> 00:08:27.284
on a different level of
introducing other artists, then,

00:08:27.284 --> 00:08:29.571
after that I became a mentor.

00:08:29.571 --> 00:08:31.571
- Right.
- So I think just to

00:08:31.571 --> 00:08:35.738
continue to evolve in a
way that is beneficial for

00:08:37.165 --> 00:08:40.379
growth of myself and others, my likeness

00:08:40.379 --> 00:08:43.103
to continue to be remembered
throughout history,

00:08:43.103 --> 00:08:46.103
and associated with something great.

00:08:48.996 --> 00:08:50.129
For me,

00:08:50.129 --> 00:08:51.462
there's a mantra

00:08:52.423 --> 00:08:53.781
that I've,

00:08:53.781 --> 00:08:55.192
I've lived by.

00:08:55.192 --> 00:08:56.442
And it is that,

00:08:57.803 --> 00:08:58.720
the journey

00:08:59.833 --> 00:09:03.908
of the destination is
really what it's all about.

00:09:03.908 --> 00:09:04.741
The

00:09:05.818 --> 00:09:07.433
pursuit

00:09:07.433 --> 00:09:11.302
is more important than
the actual destination.

00:09:11.302 --> 00:09:14.692
So as long as you are moving,
as long as you are working,

00:09:14.692 --> 00:09:17.160
that is the destination.
- Wow.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.660
- Yeah, the journey.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:21.175
Or really it is simply that,
the journey is the destination.

00:09:21.175 --> 00:09:23.151
- I agree.
- As long as you're working,

00:09:23.151 --> 00:09:24.284
you're good.

00:09:24.284 --> 00:09:26.208
- Fortunate enough to be honored at the

00:09:26.208 --> 00:09:28.861
Essence Awards Luncheon for
the Fierce and Fearless Award,

00:09:28.861 --> 00:09:30.449
and I was talking to my
girlfriend AJ Johnson

00:09:30.449 --> 00:09:34.747
who was my trainer, but
she's also a life coach,

00:09:34.747 --> 00:09:36.709
and I was like, do I tell it?

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:39.177
If I'm getting an award for
being fierce and fearless,

00:09:39.177 --> 00:09:40.777
how 'about I really be fierce and fearless

00:09:40.777 --> 00:09:43.694
and explain to people my evolution?

00:09:44.691 --> 00:09:47.267
I love who I am today but
that wasn't always the case.

00:09:47.267 --> 00:09:50.528
I didn't love my features,
I didn't love my weight,

00:09:50.528 --> 00:09:52.131
I didn't love my hair,
I didn't love my lips.

00:09:52.131 --> 00:09:56.346
And it's been an evolution,
and I wasn't always nice,

00:09:56.346 --> 00:09:58.650
or as gracious as I could've been,

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:00.082
or happy for other people.

00:10:00.082 --> 00:10:02.708
And just sort of explain that
journey through my speech.

00:10:02.708 --> 00:10:04.397
- When you build up for Formula One,

00:10:04.397 --> 00:10:06.433
you're obviously preparing to
race, but you're not prepared

00:10:06.433 --> 00:10:09.506
for what comes along with
being a Formula One driver.

00:10:09.506 --> 00:10:13.006
The pressure of such a big team, sponsors,

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:16.686
media, sitting onstage talking.

00:10:16.686 --> 00:10:18.208
You're not prepared for that.

00:10:18.208 --> 00:10:19.837
You're not put through a school

00:10:19.837 --> 00:10:21.639
or through other interviews for it.

00:10:21.639 --> 00:10:24.906
So you arrive in the deep end
without being able to swim

00:10:24.906 --> 00:10:27.389
and I mean I made a lot of mistakes.

00:10:27.389 --> 00:10:30.355
I got into, obviously
I was quick on track.

00:10:30.355 --> 00:10:33.462
That was the easy part,
it was everything outside.

00:10:33.462 --> 00:10:34.295
But,

00:10:35.189 --> 00:10:39.356
lost the first year, in
2007 by one point which was,

00:10:41.868 --> 00:10:43.802
depending on how seriously
you take your job,

00:10:43.802 --> 00:10:46.398
it was emotionally
traumatizing the first year.

00:10:46.398 --> 00:10:51.030
Came back the next year,
somehow came through that,

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:54.451
that experience, and
then in that last race,

00:10:54.451 --> 00:10:55.845
I had to finish fifth.

00:10:55.845 --> 00:10:59.475
I started third, I think
it was, and I was fourth,

00:10:59.475 --> 00:11:01.867
fifth, and then with
probably like six laps,

00:11:01.867 --> 00:11:04.902
seven laps to go or something,
I was down in sixth.

00:11:04.902 --> 00:11:07.627
And the guy that was ahead
of me was Sebastian Vettel.

00:11:07.627 --> 00:11:08.575
And,

00:11:08.575 --> 00:11:09.408
there was,

00:11:13.177 --> 00:11:14.996
I couldn't do anything even
to save my mother's life.

00:11:14.996 --> 00:11:17.095
If my mom was over there
on the edge of a cliff,

00:11:17.095 --> 00:11:18.647
I had to pass him in order to do it,

00:11:18.647 --> 00:11:20.702
I couldn't get past him. (laughing)

00:11:20.702 --> 00:11:22.710
You know, I couldn't
get past this guy and,

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:25.092
for those laps I just wasn't giving up.

00:11:25.092 --> 00:11:28.631
But I could see that dream fading away.

00:11:28.631 --> 00:11:32.716
And then the last lap, some
guy was on slick tires,

00:11:32.716 --> 00:11:35.063
I was on wets, he was stumbling,

00:11:35.063 --> 00:11:36.805
quite a few of them were stumbling.

00:11:36.805 --> 00:11:38.291
I was overtaking cars here and there.

00:11:38.291 --> 00:11:40.036
I had no idea where I was.

00:11:40.036 --> 00:11:42.108
I thought they were back markers.

00:11:42.108 --> 00:11:44.593
The guy came across the
line and thought he had,

00:11:44.593 --> 00:11:46.880
for a second was world champion,

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:49.605
and then I came across
the line 17 seconds later

00:11:49.605 --> 00:11:51.341
and I crossed the line and I thought

00:11:51.341 --> 00:11:55.005
I lost the world championship,
so my heart sunk.

00:11:55.005 --> 00:11:57.490
I was distraught, and then,

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.287
I don't know why they
took so long, but like

00:11:59.287 --> 00:12:01.838
12, 13 seconds later they
told me I was world champion.

00:12:01.838 --> 00:12:05.593
I mean I didn't know what
the hell was going on.

00:12:05.593 --> 00:12:08.182
I think just at the time, after that,

00:12:08.182 --> 00:12:10.320
big whirlwind of media,

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:12.974
back at the factory,
there was so much tension.

00:12:12.974 --> 00:12:17.767
I guess I was only 23, so
I just didn't feel I was,

00:12:17.767 --> 00:12:19.760
don't forget, growing up, instead of

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.436
hanging out with friends
on the weekends and

00:12:22.436 --> 00:12:25.638
doing normal kid's social
life stuff, I was racing.

00:12:25.638 --> 00:12:26.872
I was with adults.

00:12:26.872 --> 00:12:30.808
So, I missed that a lot, that
maturity growing up stage.

00:12:30.808 --> 00:12:33.292
I don't feel I was mature enough to really

00:12:33.292 --> 00:12:35.933
be able to embrace the whole
experience and enjoy it.

00:12:35.933 --> 00:12:37.595
So I tell you, it was not a great,

00:12:37.595 --> 00:12:39.407
it was, it's amazing that
I won the championship,

00:12:39.407 --> 00:12:41.421
but it just wasn't able to enjoy it.

00:12:41.421 --> 00:12:43.888
And rolled into the second year,

00:12:43.888 --> 00:12:45.549
the year after that for example.

00:12:45.549 --> 00:12:47.683
But the last two
championships I've really,

00:12:47.683 --> 00:12:49.262
I guess, I'm coming of an age,

00:12:49.262 --> 00:12:52.311
been able to really absorb it
and enjoy the moment because

00:12:52.311 --> 00:12:54.650
so much work has gone in for my family.

00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:56.326
I don't take it for granted,

00:12:56.326 --> 00:12:59.925
the opportunity that I have for one.

00:12:59.925 --> 00:13:02.303
There are so many people
that would cut their leg off

00:13:02.303 --> 00:13:05.136
to be in my seat and do what I do.

00:13:06.068 --> 00:13:08.589
So I make sure that I
maximize every time that I get

00:13:08.589 --> 00:13:10.558
in the car, I'm representing my family

00:13:10.558 --> 00:13:12.050
every time that I get in that car.

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:13.445
And,

00:13:13.445 --> 00:13:15.028
so there's nothing,

00:13:15.939 --> 00:13:18.689
there's no time for second place.

00:13:19.975 --> 00:13:21.795
Of course those experiences,

00:13:21.795 --> 00:13:23.093
when you have those lows like

00:13:23.093 --> 00:13:25.778
losing the world championship
only make you stronger

00:13:25.778 --> 00:13:30.126
when you do, or realize
these heights and lows.

00:13:30.126 --> 00:13:31.136
Once you've had the low,

00:13:31.136 --> 00:13:33.331
you appreciate the highs even more.

00:13:33.331 --> 00:13:34.911
- And so presumably
particularly frustrating

00:13:34.911 --> 00:13:37.688
for you this season, I
mean it's early days yet.

00:13:37.688 --> 00:13:38.884
- It's a killer season.

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:40.009
It's

00:13:40.009 --> 00:13:42.471
terrible. (laughing)

00:13:42.471 --> 00:13:46.265
Obviously had a couple of
amazing years, the last two.

00:13:46.265 --> 00:13:48.876
I would say this is, luckily through

00:13:48.876 --> 00:13:52.079
the experience of the 10
years of racing you kind of,

00:13:52.079 --> 00:13:54.667
you have the ups and downs
and I definitely think

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:57.309
these past five races have been

00:13:57.309 --> 00:13:59.723
massively testing for myself, my mechanics

00:13:59.723 --> 00:14:01.135
for my engineers.

00:14:01.135 --> 00:14:03.580
I think each time I see
it as a challenge to rise.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:05.518
I see it as a challenge to, you know,

00:14:05.518 --> 00:14:06.681
I'm going to be facing the media right now

00:14:06.681 --> 00:14:08.761
but I feel terrible, I'm
angry that I lost the race

00:14:08.761 --> 00:14:10.091
or something like that.

00:14:10.091 --> 00:14:12.673
But it's a moment for me to,

00:14:12.673 --> 00:14:15.146
kids that are watching, to
me to say the right things.

00:14:15.146 --> 00:14:17.673
It's a moment for me to lift my guys up

00:14:17.673 --> 00:14:20.122
who are probably feeling
just as much as me.

00:14:20.122 --> 00:14:23.925
Or back in the factory who
work non-stop to build my car.

00:14:23.925 --> 00:14:26.008
So so much going on, and,

00:14:27.814 --> 00:14:31.285
I feel, often when I do it right,

00:14:31.285 --> 00:14:34.010
I feel, I come out of it so much stronger.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:37.630
And so, I do feel this is just
a trials and tribulations.

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:41.268
This is a period of time
of growth for me that,

00:14:41.268 --> 00:14:43.143
whilst there's always growth, you know,

00:14:43.143 --> 00:14:45.310
I met Nelson Mandela once,

00:14:47.294 --> 00:14:50.634
when he was 90, for his 90th
birthday, and he said to me,

00:14:50.634 --> 00:14:52.373
that he was still
learning at that time so,

00:14:52.373 --> 00:14:54.584
- Wow.
- I have a long way to go.

00:14:54.584 --> 00:14:55.532
Hopefully.

00:14:55.532 --> 00:14:56.863
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:14:56.863 --> 00:14:58.025
I hope you enjoyed.

00:14:58.025 --> 00:14:59.889
I love to know what
was your favorite clip?

00:14:59.889 --> 00:15:01.525
What resonated the most with you?

00:15:01.525 --> 00:15:02.998
What are you going to take from this video

00:15:02.998 --> 00:15:06.567
and immediately apply to your
life or your business somehow?

00:15:06.567 --> 00:15:07.873
Please leave it down in the comments,

00:15:07.873 --> 00:15:09.260
I'm super curious to find out.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:10.655
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:15:10.655 --> 00:15:13.638
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:15:13.638 --> 00:15:17.193
and whatever your One Word is, much love.

00:15:17.193 --> 00:15:18.693
I'll see you soon.

